From 18fa5c82a9a1501c608568236bc5f52b4d311106 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Machado?= <machaddr@falanet.org>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 15:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: expose CPU compatible as model name
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

RISC-V exports the first CPU compatible string as "uarch" in
/proc/cpuinfo.  Several established userspace consumers, including libgtop
and screenfetch, only recognize the conventional "model name" key and leave
the processor identity empty on otherwise correctly described systems.

Expose the same standardized CPU compatible value through "model name" as
an additional compatibility field.  Preserve "uarch" and all existing
RISC-V cpuinfo fields unchanged.

On JH7110 this identifies each application hart as sifive,u74-mc, matching
the CPU compatible in the upstream device tree binding.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: André Machado <machaddr@falanet.org>
---
 arch/riscv/kernel/cpu.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/kernel/cpu.c b/arch/riscv/kernel/cpu.c
index c6eb606d5ac0..c1520d002c46 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/kernel/cpu.c
+++ b/arch/riscv/kernel/cpu.c
@@ -326,8 +326,10 @@ static int c_show(struct seq_file *m, void *v)
 		node = of_get_cpu_node(cpu_id, NULL);
 
 		if (!of_property_read_string(node, "compatible", &compat) &&
-		    strcmp(compat, "riscv"))
+		    strcmp(compat, "riscv")) {
+			seq_printf(m, "model name\t: %s\n", compat);
 			seq_printf(m, "uarch\t\t: %s\n", compat);
+		}
 
 		of_node_put(node);
 	}
